                <pb facs="0417" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/355a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-13T20:00:00-04:00">September 13,
                            1939—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>118. Following conversations regarding which you are being informed by air pouch,
                    a basis has been agreed upon with Gazitua for announcement of trade-agreement
                    negotiations with Chile, possibly in about 3 weeks. It is understood that the
                    proposed basis has been submitted to his Government for consideration.</p>
                <p>The basis leaves the exchange control question open for discussion in the light
                    of the Chilean situation at the time of negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
